Build Cargo build scripts in the plain tool configuration

A build script is compiled in a tool configuration that takes the
compilation mode of the crate it serves, so in any mode but the one tools are
built in, build scripts get a tool configuration of their own, and with it
another analysis of the toolchains and crates they depend on. In the plain
tool configuration they share the one the other tools use. A script still
learns the crate's mode: cargo_build_script sets PROFILE, DEBUG and OPT_LEVEL
from its own configuration, which is the crate's.

The transition that applied the crate's mode stays defined, unused, to keep
the patch to one line.

The patch changes one line of the file and carries the six around it, too
little of the file to attribute.

